1
00:00:06,131 --> 00:00:08,133
["Strange Days" playing]

2
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:15,515
♪ These are the strange days ♪ 

3
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:22,439
♪ Life plays out in the strangest way ♪

4
00:00:24,941 --> 00:00:29,779
♪ I want what you want ♪

5
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:31,740
♪ To be alright ♪

6
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,033
♪ To be noticed ♪

7
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:35,827
♪ To find my place ♪

8
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:41,291
♪ Oh… ♪

9
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,084
[dog whimpering]

10
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:45,462
[Chrishell sighs]

11
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:48,506
-[knocking]
-[dog barks]

12
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:49,549
[Chrishell] Coming.

13
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:54,262
-[Chrishell] Hi.
-Hi. Honey.

14
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,389
[Mary sighs]

15
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,475
-How are you?
-This is so beautiful.

16
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:00,101
-Here.
-Thank you.

17
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:02,020
-Come on, Grace.
-I want another hug.

18
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:05,440
I just wanted to give you a hug so bad.
[groans]

19
00:01:05,732 --> 00:01:07,734
-[Mary] How are you?
-[Chrishell] I've been better.

20
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:08,818
Not gonna lie.

21
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:12,363
[sighs] What... What happened?

22
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:15,241
I'm sorry.

23
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:19,204
[groans] Okay.

24
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,831
[sigh] I just have to…

25
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:24,459
Fuck. I don't know.

26
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:27,420
I just feel like, um…

27
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:32,300
Sorry, I'm just kinda in shock
with it all, so…

28
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:34,719
I'm trying to, like…

29
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,890
keep it together,
but it's just a lot all at once

30
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:43,186
'cause everybody in the whole world knows,
like, at the same time that I knew, so…

31
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,104
I know.

32
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:47,232
Have you ever been knocked over by a wave,
and you don't know which way to swim 

33
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:48,900
-to get up?
-I know that feeling.

34
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,528
I've been there,
and I wouldn't wish it on anybody.

35
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,113
Yeah.

36
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:57,367
I don't think anyone ever gets married,
thinking that they'll ever get a divorce.

37
00:01:57,450 --> 00:02:00,203
I'm definitely a hopeless romantic.

38
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:03,373
And I feel stupid
even saying that out loud.

39
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:06,125
I-I'm so confused.

40
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:11,131
At the charity event, like,
he donated all this stuff. Like, what--

41
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:14,092
[Chrishell] You wanna see
what our donation items are?

42
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:17,762
This is an Annie Leibovitz signed poster.
And then coffee with Justin Hartley.

43
00:02:17,846 --> 00:02:19,264
This is my husband, by the way.

44
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:20,932
We were totally fine that day.

45
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,144
I mean, I thought we were totally fine.

46
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:26,771
Did you get in an argument or anything?

47
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:28,273
We had a fight that morning

48
00:02:28,356 --> 00:02:31,359
over the phone, and I had--
I never saw him since.

49
00:02:31,442 --> 00:02:33,194
We didn't talk things through and…

50
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:38,032
Before we had a chance
to figure anything out, he filed.

51
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:41,911
[sniffles]

52
00:02:47,417 --> 00:02:48,835
[Mary] How did you find out?

53
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:52,005
Did he, like, just come talk to you
out of the blue or what?

54
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:55,633
[Chrishell sniffles]

55
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,971
Um, I found out…

56
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:02,348
because he texted me.

57
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:06,728
That we were filed.

58
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,063
He texted you?

59
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:14,152
Forty-five minutes later, the world knew.

60
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:15,737
He just blindsided you?

61
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:20,533
[Chrishell] Because of the crazy way
in which this went down,

62
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,076
people want answers.

63
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,494
And…

64
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:26,831
I fucking want answers.

65
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,459
That's shitty.

66
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:31,085
Like, beyond shitty.

67
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:35,590
I know people are saying
we were only married two years,

68
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:39,552
-but we were together for six years.
-You deserve more respect than that.

69
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:43,640
In a fight, like, that's his go-to.
You know, like, I'm out, I'm out.

70
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:48,436
I hate that kind of impulsive stuff,
but I always just thought, you know,

71
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:50,313
that's just an issue
that we work through it.

72
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:54,984
Part of a relationship, you talk about it
and, you know, compromise and try

73
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:58,863
and change for the other person.
But those are two different things.

74
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:02,492
Getting upset and going down
to the courthouse and filing…

75
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:03,785
that's huge.

76
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:07,205
If that's really what he wanted,
there are better ways to go about.

77
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:09,499
Yeah. Have you talked to him?

78
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,084
Like, at all, since?

79
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:15,171
Well, I talked to him right after,
'cause I thought that must be a joke.

80
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,840
But that was kind of the end
of the communication.

81
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:20,510
What am I supposed to say?
What do you say after that?

82
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:23,179
It's like,
now I have to find a place to live.

83
00:04:24,764 --> 00:04:27,809
Now I have to scramble
and figure this out, you know?

84
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:30,311
When I found out, I was…

85
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:33,523
um, minutes before leaving the house
for work.

86
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:36,609
So I immediately just grabbed a few things
and I--

87
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:39,779
And I just got out of there
as fast as I could. I didn't…

88
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:44,826
I don't think I really knew
where I was going

89
00:04:44,909 --> 00:04:48,162
or what I was gonna do,
but I-- I just had to-- to leave.

90
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:50,915
Is it going through attorneys
or something now? Or…

91
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,459
[sighs] Oh my God. It's so weird.

92
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:56,546
Like, whose life am I living?
I've never had an attorney in my life.

93
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:57,964
I, like, wha--?

94
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:01,884
I don't even know-- It's just so strange.

95
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:05,346
[Mary] Going through a divorce,
it's emotionally draining.

96
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,681
It's almost like a death.

97
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,809
It's like someone that you are so used to
spending so much time with,

98
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:12,937
and you can't see them.
They're out of your life.

99
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:16,024
But it's worse than death because not only
are they out of your life,

100
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:19,110
but then you're fighting over money.
You're fighting over assets.

101
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,988
It's probably one of the worst things
you can go through.

102
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:26,075
-Sorry, this is so depressing. I'm sorry.
-[Mary] No! Oh my God.

103
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:29,162
[sighs] Fuck.

104
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:31,456
I just--

105
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:33,791
Is there anything I can do?

106
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,836
Uh, this is it. I really appreciate it.

107
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:41,549
When I think of marriage, I think of…
you know, you work on things with people

108
00:05:41,632 --> 00:05:42,967
if they're not perfect.

109
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:45,053
No one is, you work on it.

110
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:47,764
You talk about it.

111
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:50,516
You… [scoffs]

112
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:53,519
[scoffs]

113
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,314
I just-- You don't throw out--

114
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,317
You don't go out
looking for greener grass.

115
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:02,403
Sometimes you have to water the grass
that you have.

116
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:04,405
And that's what marriage is.

117
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:07,533
You know, sometimes it can be hard.
I mean, I don't think…

118
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:11,204
it should be more hard than easy,
I mean, at all.

119
00:06:11,287 --> 00:06:13,956
But that's why I'm so confused, 'cause…

120
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,835
I didn't feel like that balance was off.

121
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:21,756
I just feel stupid.

122
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:32,308
It's hard, like, it takes a toll on,
like, your self-worth,

123
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:36,604
where you just feel, like, the anger.
Like, how could you do it this way?

124
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:40,400
And then, the sadness of, like,
I love him so much,

125
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,069
this was my best friend.
Who do I talk to now?

126
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:47,740
Just, like, such a… roller coaster.

127
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:52,036
["Hurricane" playing]
♪ Comin' like a hurricane ♪

128
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:55,456
♪ I take it in real slow ♪

129
00:06:58,167 --> 00:07:00,169
♪ I don't know ♪

130
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,925
[upbeat pop music playing]
♪ It ain't over 'til I say it is ♪

131
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:09,846
♪ It's ain't over
'Til my heart stops beating ♪

132
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:13,224
♪ Can't stop me
No, you can't stop me ♪

133
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:16,561
♪ High climbing
I go ahead at full speed ♪

134
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:19,063
♪ Don't slow down
Don't slow down ♪

135
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:23,151
♪ You can try your best
But you can't stop me… ♪

136
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:31,742
-[Davina] Hello? Knock, knock.
-[Christine] Hello! Come in.

137
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,369
I'm in here.

138
00:07:34,537 --> 00:07:35,913
-Hi, babe.
-Hi!

139
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:37,206
-You look so cute.
-How are you?

140
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,833
-Good.
-You look great.

141
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:40,543
-Hey.
-Hi, honey, how are you?

142
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:43,462
-How are you doing?
-Good. So I need help with my Keurig,

143
00:07:43,546 --> 00:07:46,174
because of my nails
I can't push the Continue button.

144
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:48,301
-Can someone push Continue?
-[Maya] Sure.

145
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:51,637
-Shit. Okay.
-[Christine] I'm making tea.

146
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,764
-[Davina] Are you making something?
-Yeah, tea.

147
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:54,932
I'm like, are you cooking?

148
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,018
[Christine, Davina] It's not working?

149
00:07:57,101 --> 00:08:00,396
-[repeats] I'll just do the microwave.
-[Davina] Living the dream.

150
00:08:00,479 --> 00:08:02,523
I thought you were cooking for a second.

151
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,816
-I was like, no…
-Well, yeah.

152
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,736
It's tea time, bitches.
I am cooking, actually.

153
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:10,948
Listen, it's not really hot,
but I'm not saying I'm Wolfgang, okay?

154
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:12,408
But it'll work for now.

155
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:14,410
[laughs] You actually look a lot
like Wolfgang,

156
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,204
-I was getting confused.
-I thought so too.

157
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:17,371
-Yeah.
-[Davina] Let's do it.

158
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:21,667
Honestly, this whole thing with Chrishell
just made me… I'm shocked.

159
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:25,004
The article came out,
and I thought it was a joke.

160
00:08:25,087 --> 00:08:27,006
[Maya] I'm so disappointed too, like--

161
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:29,342
I mean, it was like a ton of bricks,
like--

162
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:31,636
You don't know what to say.
You're just in shock.

163
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:34,347
Like, I don't think any of us
had any idea, like--

164
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:37,516
You know, she's not very open.
Like, we're so open with our stuff,

165
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,686
and I don't know him, and he has his side
of the story too probably.

166
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:43,731
-So I don't know.
-We're only hearing one side of the story.

167
00:08:43,814 --> 00:08:47,109
-[Davina] Yeah.
-So I'm trying to do my best to--

168
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:50,488
[both] Be open-minded
and considerate too, yeah.

169
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:53,115
Look, someone might have done
something wrong,

170
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:56,536
we can't assume and just judge.
And it's none of our business and--

171
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:57,995
-It's not.
-…maybe she'll tell us--

172
00:08:58,079 --> 00:09:00,248
-Yeah.
-…maybe she won't. We have to obviously

173
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:02,333
respect her and their privacy.

174
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:05,461
I'm sure it's awful, like,
devastating for both of them.

175
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:09,340
It's hard to be unconditionally supportive
and 100 percent Team Chrishell

176
00:09:09,423 --> 00:09:12,051
when she's so guarded
and so protective all the time.

177
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:16,055
It's really tricky
to understand if she's blindsided or not.

178
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:18,516
We don't know any details of anything.

179
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:19,934
It's so crazy, yeah.

180
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:23,479
-It's just so wild.
-To me, Justin and Chrishell were perfect.

181
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:25,189
They were a good-looking couple,

182
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,858
-look happy and they just--
-[Davina] You don't know, right?

183
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:30,695
And I don't know Justin,
but from when I met Justin

184
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,905
he seems like a very cool nice guy--

185
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:34,490
-I know.
-…she talked highly of him--

186
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:35,992
He was always nice to us--

187
00:09:36,075 --> 00:09:37,618
So what the heck happened?

188
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:41,622
I don't know what he's going through,
I don't know how he's feeling--

189
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:44,959
I wanna ask her,
"Did you really have, like, zero idea?"

190
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:48,087
-Do you think you'd get the real answer?
-Probably not.

191
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:54,010
I believe, in my opinion,
that it's something that has been ongoing.

192
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:57,805
I don't believe
someone just files out of the blue

193
00:09:57,888 --> 00:10:00,641
because you had a fight or a bad day.

194
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,518
I don't think anyone has zero idea.

195
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,770
-Yeah, that's how I feel.
-Something happened.

196
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:06,856
I read an article that said that

197
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:11,193
Justin's sisters unfollowed Chrishell
on Instagram.

198
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:12,987
The thing is, like, why? Right?

199
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:15,031
Then the questions
all start into whys again.

200
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:18,868
[Maya] Davina and Christine think
Chrishell wasn't blindsided.

201
00:10:18,951 --> 00:10:21,829
I think, personally,
she probably was blindsided.

202
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:22,997
But, uh…

203
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,499
Who knows? You know what?

204
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,543
All we can do is just support and--

205
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:31,047
-[Davina] That's it.
-Every article that I have seen her in

206
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:33,466
has always been "Justin Hartley's wife."

207
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:37,595
I hope she forms her own identity,
you know. I want that for her.

208
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:39,513
Do you?

209
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:43,768
I do. Honestly, I'm excited for her to be
Chrishell Strauss.

210
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:45,519
Stause.

211
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:46,937
Stause? Strauss?

212
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:48,773
S-T-A-U-S-E.

213
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,858
Stause? Isn't there an "r" in there?

214
00:10:50,941 --> 00:10:52,693
I thought it said Strauss too,
but it's not.

215
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:54,904
-It's without an "r."
-It's Stause? Stause?

216
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:58,074
-Is it Stause?
-Hey, guys! She should keep Hartley

217
00:10:58,157 --> 00:11:00,117
-'cause it's easier.
-[Davina] Guys, no.

218
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:02,745
["Can You Feel It?" playing]

219
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:06,540
♪ Can you feel it? ♪

220
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:10,503
♪ Can you feel it? ♪

221
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,341
♪ Can you feel it? ♪

222
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:19,887
[knocking]

223
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,263
[Amanza] Honey, I'm home.

224
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,140
-[Heather] Is it locked?
-[Amanza] Yeah.

225
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:24,517
I forgot my key.

226
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:28,562
[Heather] Oh, sorry, I guess I thought
this was my house now. [laughs]

227
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,147
Hi. Oh my God.

228
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,274
-Right?
-Whoa. It's so clean and--

229
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,651
It really came together.

230
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:36,028
-This looks amazing.
-Jason's gonna be happy. 

231
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:38,656
What do you think?
-[Amanza] Heck yeah. These are fun.

232
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:41,826
Heather and I are working
together to stage the Fennell house,

233
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,120
but the renovation took longer
than we expected,

234
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:47,289
and I wasn't able to help her pick out
the artwork. So…

235
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:51,252
I really hope we don't run into any kinks
tonight because we have to get this done.

236
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:54,088
There's one, two, three, four, five.
So, six.

237
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:58,509
-Is this all of it or are there more?
-[Heather] I had chose… eight.

238
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:02,722
Maybe they must have sold
because she… well, she didn't tell me.

239
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,641
So I don't know,
I'm a little frustrated, but…

240
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,893
[Amanza] Maybe we should start
placing it and seeing

241
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,437
if it's actually gonna work.

242
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,398
We just need to figure out
if we have enough and--

243
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:15,609
and hang 'em and see
what fits best where, you know?

244
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,695
I probably would've made sure

245
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:23,242
that there was way more art
than necessary, but I'm gonna fix it.

246
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:27,329
Sometimes I'm late…
but I know how to stage a house.

247
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:29,039
That's what I do. Problem solved.

248
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:32,293
I would say because of size,
this one needs to go here

249
00:12:32,376 --> 00:12:33,461
because of the scale.

250
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:35,171
[Heather] What about the dining table?

251
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:37,590
That needs to be pretty big,
so the other biggest one.

252
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,467
Then where would this one go?

253
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:42,011
-Oh, above the master.
-The master.

254
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:44,722
[Heather] I am not good
at hanging paintings

255
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:47,641
because I can never find
the little hook thing.

256
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:50,019
Okay, you know what?
I'm just gonna go in here

257
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,272
because I really think
this needs to go in the office. [giggles]

258
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,526
Shockingly, Amanza and I
are actually getting along.

259
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,404
We're working well together,
and I've seen her really step up.

260
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:03,115
So I'm proud of her,
and I think we got this.

261
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:07,119
I think maybe…
we could scoot the bar thing over.

262
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:10,372
-It's kind of tall, you know.
-[Heather] Okay. Oh God! [squeals]

263
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:14,502
And I'm actually having fun with her,
which is very shocking.

264
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:17,796
It looks like we're robbing the place
in white gloves, aren't we?

265
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:19,882
Is that our--?

266
00:13:19,965 --> 00:13:20,883
Right on.

267
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,384
Ta-da!

268
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:24,595
It's on.
I don't know if it's even, but it's on.

269
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,515
-I think it's even.
-[Amanza] Is it?

270
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:30,017
No, now it's not.
I was gonna say something really stupid.

271
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,562
I was, like, maybe we should turn it,
but it's a square, right?

272
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:40,694
-[Heather] Have you talked to Chrishell?
-A few little voice memos, and…

273
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:44,073
like, brief conversation,
but I haven't seen her.

274
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:45,824
And how she doing?

275
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:48,202
Like, she's devastated, she's heartbroken.

276
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:52,206
I'll hopefully get to talk to her
and get more details when she's ready,

277
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,791
but what the fuck?

278
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:56,544
-I feel so bad.
-[Amanza] I feel so bad for her too, yeah.

279
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:59,797
I'm such a lover,
and I believe in true love,

280
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,174
and so it's, you know, it's really sad.

281
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:06,512
It makes me think too, 'cause I,
you know, I'm in Tarek's kids' life,

282
00:14:06,595 --> 00:14:11,517
and then she was a stepmom to his daughter
and so close with her and--

283
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,476
It's so scary.

284
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,062
…you feel that bond, and now
it's just taken away.

285
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:19,233
Heather's realizing now how sensitive,
how delicate these situations can be.

286
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:22,987
This wasn't supposed to be a sad moment.
[laughs]

287
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:25,114
We can't cry on this painting. Like…

288
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:27,533
[Heather] Our make-up is gonna be
all over it.

289
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:31,996
-[Heather] Is it on?
-Yeah.

290
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,541
[Amanza] That actually looks
really good there.

291
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:38,502
[Heather] I honestly think
Jason is gonna be super happy with us.

292
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:41,589
[down-tempo pop music playing]

293
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:45,301
♪ Oh oh oh oh all the time ♪

294
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:52,182
♪ Oh oh oh oh all life… ♪

295
00:14:55,936 --> 00:14:57,688
[Mary] Do you have a few minutes?

296
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:02,776
This situation with Chrishell and Justin,
like, has really…

297
00:15:03,944 --> 00:15:05,863
-It's really hit me.
-How is she doing?

298
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:07,906
I mean…

299
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,993
-Not okay, but she will be.
-Yeah, poor thing.

300
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:14,872
It's to be expected. She's strong.
She'll pull through, and she'll be great.

301
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:17,333
-But right now, it just…
-Suck.

302
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:18,500
Who would be okay?

303
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:20,336
Relationships…

304
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:23,047
like, need a solid foundation.

305
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:28,385
And we haven't really had a chance
to talk about the whole Vegas thing.

306
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:30,596
-[Romain] Mm-hmm.
-Obviously, I was pretty…

307
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:33,015
-Am I in trouble? [laughs]
-Pretty ups--

308
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:35,267
Yes.

309
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:39,229
My only rule was you don't
have girls come back up to the room.

310
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,939
I didn't. Don't blame that on me.

311
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:43,150
-I--
-That's not my fault if we have a suite.

312
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,777
I never bring anyone.

313
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:47,696
So I respect your rules.

314
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,408
Uh, how is the respect when I asked,

315
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:53,327
"Were there girls up there?"
and you lied?

316
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:56,372
-Where was the respect then?
-I didn't think it was the right thing

317
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:57,456
to tell you at that point.

318
00:15:57,539 --> 00:16:00,751
[Mary] Lying is a very sensitive thing
to me.

319
00:16:00,834 --> 00:16:03,712
It led ultimately to my divorce,

320
00:16:03,796 --> 00:16:06,382
and I don't want
to go down that path again.

321
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:09,176
Romain's a very,
what I thought was, trustworthy guy,

322
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:11,971
and this stupid lie has…

323
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:15,224
It's made me question everything.

324
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:17,601
-[Romain] I didn't want to lie.
-But you did lie

325
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:19,770
-when I asked you--
-Yes, let me finish.

326
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,564
I did it for a good reason,

327
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:25,859
'cause I don't want you
to get hurt just a week before, right?

328
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:28,529
But do you see what it looks like?
When you hadn't said anything--

329
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:30,447
-I know.
-…and I find out from somebody else?

330
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:32,282
Do you see what that looks like?

331
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:35,244
Why would you lie
if you didn't do anything?

332
00:16:35,744 --> 00:16:37,955
-You were so stressed--
-[Mary] I understand,

333
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:41,041
but do you see how a lie like that--

334
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,836
-Yeah, I do, I do get it.
-…makes me question everything?

335
00:16:43,919 --> 00:16:47,006
Have you lied about other things?
Have you… Can I actually trust you?

336
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:50,968
So my brain is, like…
going and going and going, thinking,

337
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:54,805
is this the same person
that I thought you were?

338
00:16:54,888 --> 00:17:00,060
I have more respect if you own it,
if you mess up, you own it and come to me.

339
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:03,605
I can hate what you did.
I can be mad at you.

340
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:07,693
Hell, yeah, I'm going to be mad at you,
but at least I still have trust.

341
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:10,112
It's scary.

342
00:17:10,195 --> 00:17:14,199
Yeah, I do get your point. But you can't
put back everything in question.

343
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:16,118
-No.
-That's what a lie does--

344
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:19,288
[Romain] Yes, but then when you get
to know the whole story.

345
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:20,706
It's wrong what I've done.

346
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:24,209
But I don't want you to freak out
because I knew you would.

347
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:27,254
Like, it's not like
I was trying to hide something bad.

348
00:17:27,838 --> 00:17:29,965
It's still--
Those thoughts go through your head

349
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:33,677
once-- once you've lied like that
about something…

350
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:35,804
pretty shady.

351
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,307
I mean, that's not cool.

352
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:42,603
At this point, I really feel like…

353
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:47,483
like I don't know if I can trust him.

354
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,485
["Big Bad Wolf" playing]

355
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:53,781
♪ Living like kings comes with a price ♪

356
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:57,826
♪ You're rollin' in riches
Then you're rollin' the dice ♪

357
00:17:58,368 --> 00:18:00,788
♪ Ain't it
No ♪

358
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:04,208
♪ Nothing's ever free
No, nothing's ever free ♪

359
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:07,252
♪ Is it?
Is it? ♪

360
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:10,798
♪ When the big bad wolf
Comes running around ♪

361
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:14,510
♪ Baby, get yourself right outta of town ♪

362
00:18:14,593 --> 00:18:17,805
♪ Royal hearts are meant to break ♪

363
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:21,517
♪ 'Cause everybody's got
A big debt to pay… ♪

364
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,478
[dog barking]

365
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:30,692
Okay, just straight back here,
to the left. Thank you very much.

366
00:18:35,072 --> 00:18:39,910
♪ Stuck in the head
Falling deeper down, down, down… ♪

367
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:41,328
-[knocking]
-[dog barking]

368
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:43,580
[both] Hi.

369
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,253
-Thank you.
 -You look pretty.

370
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:52,130
This is sweet, thank you.

371
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,799
-Well…
-It's been a rough day.

372
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:56,426
-Rough week.
-Just what I needed.

373
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:59,263
And I think that's maybe
a big enough glass.

374
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:00,556
Oh my God.

375
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,268
Let's try it. Let's…

376
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:07,312
I could use it today. I'm not gonna lie.
[groans]

377
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:10,816
[Amanza] I've been through a divorce.
It's… it's brutal.

378
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:13,360
Especially the moving day.

379
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:16,029
Because that's when it really gets real.

380
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:19,700
When you're separating furniture
and walking around your old house,

381
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:21,869
trying to figure out what to take
and what to keep,

382
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:24,621
and it's just, like, it's final.

383
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:25,539
This doesn't--

384
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:26,832
-I love that.
-Really?

385
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:28,792
-No, this I love.
-[Amanza] Oh my God.

386
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:31,670
Are you kidding? That was one
of the points. I thought it was a sign

387
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,005
it was, like, perfect.

388
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:35,966
I hate you. I have to figure out
how to turn it on. [laughs]

389
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:39,178
I wanted to be there for her
because that transition is hard.

390
00:19:39,761 --> 00:19:42,681
She's just trying to move on and heal.

391
00:19:42,764 --> 00:19:45,142
And she can't even get away
from the public eye.

392
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,063
Oh my gosh.

393
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,983
-Well, welcome to my new… home.
-Your new home.

394
00:19:53,066 --> 00:19:56,069
So I'm gonna change the curtains,
but for now--

395
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:58,197
I've decorated the room in my head
five times since--

396
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,198
I'm definitely
gonna be able to use your help,

397
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:04,077
but there's paparazzi following me
from the house to here.

398
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:06,121
I'm impressed with how--

399
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,123
But don't judge right now.
I'm gonna change that.

400
00:20:08,206 --> 00:20:09,875
There's no-- This is a no-judgment zone.

401
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:11,293
[both] Cheers.

402
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:14,588
-Thank you.
-Obviously, I've been through a divorce,

403
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:17,883
and I just-- I'm so impressed
with how fast you got moved in.

404
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:21,261
Like, I literally, when I moved out
from my husband,

405
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:23,138
that was the part that made me break down.

406
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,974
I just remember it sucks.

407
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:30,229
[Chrishell] I just got my stuff,
and I got out of there as fast as I could.

408
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:34,608
I mean, I'm literally just barely…
getting everything together, so…

409
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:37,277
And I'm… I'm so sorry.

410
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:40,405
And I don't think there's anything

411
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:43,033
that anybody can say
to make it better right now, but…

412
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:46,370
I've got two big ears
and a big old shoulder to cry on.

413
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:54,002
I hadn't thought about a plan B, like…

414
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,714
I'm… madly in love with him.

415
00:20:57,798 --> 00:21:00,133
That's the part that sucks.
I'm like, what?

416
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,929
I don't know how you're holding up
as well as you are. I mean--

417
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:05,931
-Today was a big day--
-[Amanza] Yeah, of course.

418
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:08,850
…with the moving
and the paparazzi on top of that.

419
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:13,563
Like, that's an added thing, and, like,
just going through the photos and…

420
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:15,941
our stuff of like…

421
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:19,027
All the things that…

422
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,156
we had and he promised.

423
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:27,703
I want to hide under a rock
until this all goes away.

424
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:31,164
What about, uh…

425
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:33,959
his daughter. You talk to her?

426
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:36,795
I love her so much, and…

427
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:40,173
I had to write a letter to her, like…

428
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:41,300
Oh my God.

429
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:44,219
Sorry.

430
00:21:47,306 --> 00:21:48,307
[Chrishell sniffles]

431
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,349
[Amanza] C'mere.

432
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:53,353
[Chrishell] I don't wanna be crying.
[sniffles]

433
00:21:57,774 --> 00:21:58,775
[groans]

434
00:21:58,859 --> 00:21:59,818
[dog whines]

435
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:01,320
I'm so sorry.

436
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:06,700
Oh my God, that's my old house.
Someone's at the door.

437
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,870
-Paparazzi?
-I still have to take this off my phone.

438
00:22:09,953 --> 00:22:11,663
-When someone rings the--
-Yeah.

439
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,583
…the bell, it comes on my phone.

440
00:22:14,666 --> 00:22:16,668
I'm still getting packages to the house.

441
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,962
Like, that's how fast this was.
I literally--

442
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:23,341
I'm still getting stuff that I had ordered
before I knew anything, like, coming in.

443
00:22:24,092 --> 00:22:26,178
I'm-- it makes me so mad…

444
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:31,350
because this all could have been avoided,
you know, if we'd done this privately.

445
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:34,644
My mind is blown
that he would think that this is the…

446
00:22:34,978 --> 00:22:37,522
the way to conduct himself, but…

447
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:41,234
I can't even imagine.
I mean, just going through a divorce…

448
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:46,531
privately is tremendously heartbreaking
and overwhelming, and…

449
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:48,700
But at the end of the day,

450
00:22:48,784 --> 00:22:54,164
there can't be
one person fighting for a relationship.

451
00:22:54,247 --> 00:22:56,291
-Yeah.
-You have to have two people.

452
00:22:56,708 --> 00:23:01,421
And I think a lot has changed
in the six years that we were together

453
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:05,175
And in the two years that we were married,
like, a lot has changed, and…

454
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:08,595
Well, his-- I mean, I didn't know him
before, but his life has--

455
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:10,722
Just went, like, sky high.

456
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:13,517
I don't know what that does
to somebody's head or to their…

457
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:14,601
But, like…

458
00:23:15,268 --> 00:23:17,312
I didn't care about that stuff.

459
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:20,315
And I met him before all of that.

460
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:21,233
Yeah.

461
00:23:22,484 --> 00:23:24,986
To you, he's the same person, but…

462
00:23:25,362 --> 00:23:26,863
maybe to him it was…

463
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:30,200
a lot fast, and maybe he couldn't…

464
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,288
I can't talk about it, I'm sorry.

465
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:37,124
-It's still really hard.
-It's okay.

466
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:39,876
-Don't say anything more than you want.
-[Chrishell] It's annoying--

467
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:40,961
I know.

468
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:43,505
And then you get rid of the people that…

469
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:45,465
[Chrishell sniffles]

470
00:23:45,549 --> 00:23:48,093
That have been there for you
and helped you climb.

471
00:23:48,176 --> 00:23:50,053
'Cause one day that's gonna go away.

472
00:23:51,012 --> 00:23:51,847
And--

473
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:56,726
It just sucks because I feel like…

474
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:02,149
outer elements have reared their ugly head

475
00:24:02,232 --> 00:24:05,819
and inserted themselves
into our relationship that…

476
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:09,865
You know, these aren't normal things.

477
00:24:09,948 --> 00:24:14,870
It's not normal to meet somebody
and then they become wildly famous

478
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:18,039
or they become wildly rich
or all these things, it's like--

479
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:22,127
I don't, at the end of the day,
think that those things matter.

480
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:25,464
[sighs] And I can understand, like…

481
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:29,384
God forbid…

482
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:33,513
your feelings obviously changed for me
at some point, but…

483
00:24:34,848 --> 00:24:37,100
I just feel like
that's how you would treat…

484
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:39,728
the garbage that you throw out.

485
00:24:46,651 --> 00:24:50,447
I know it is lame and cliché to say
everything happens for a reason, but…

486
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:52,741
it does make me think of, like,

487
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:55,076
things that I bended on for him.

488
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:58,038
I had a plan, but then I met him.

489
00:24:58,121 --> 00:25:01,291
And I loved him so much,
so I changed my plan for him.

490
00:25:03,084 --> 00:25:03,919
So…

491
00:25:04,878 --> 00:25:08,715
it just makes me think,
then maybe there's a bigger plan for me.

492
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:13,970
That's a really great way to look at it,
and that is all… the truth.

493
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:16,223
But you still fucking hurt.

494
00:25:16,306 --> 00:25:20,602
But I see your survivor mechanisms
kicking in.

495
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:23,605
And I feel like
we have similar childhoods,

496
00:25:23,688 --> 00:25:26,733
and we have some-- some gritty shit
that people don't know,

497
00:25:26,816 --> 00:25:29,402
and it's made, I think,
both of us really strong.

498
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:31,488
And I can see it in you, and I admire it.

499
00:25:32,572 --> 00:25:35,158
Just make sure you tell yourself that too.

500
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:37,077
Thanks, babe.

501
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:39,120
[down-tempo pop music playing]

502
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:43,166
♪ There's no runnin' from this ♪

503
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:46,086
♪ No more hiding from the daylight ♪

504
00:25:46,169 --> 00:25:48,672
♪ Seen it comin' for a long time ♪

505
00:25:48,755 --> 00:25:51,007
♪ Get ready now
Get ready now ♪

506
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:54,886
